course: dictionary
lesson: 5138
title: Things we do without choosing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you whether something was chosen. Involuntary means done without meaning to, or without control. «I gave an involuntary yawn during the maths lesson.» Nobody decides to yawn; the body just does it, so involuntary is the right word.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «A song stuck in your head is called an earworm, and most people get them.» You did not choose to hear that song again and again, so scientists call it involuntary musical imagery. Ask yourself: did someone decide this? If not, the word may mean involuntary.
explain: In formal writing, involuntary can mean done against someone's will. «Involuntary separation» is an official US phrase for being fired from a job. The worker did not choose to leave. The meaning depends on the situation, so read the whole sentence carefully.
fact: Involuntary means done without meaning to or without control.
fact: Examples of involuntary actions are sneezing, shivering, blinking and your heartbeat.
fact: Voluntary means done by choice, so it is the opposite of involuntary.
fact: «Involuntary muscles», such as the heart, work without you thinking about them.
fact: «Involuntary separation» (official US) means being fired from a job against your will.
exercise: «I gave an involuntary yawn during the maths lesson.» What does involuntary mean here? | *Done without meaning to | Very loud and noisy | Done with great care | Done on purpose to make the class laugh
exercise: «The worker received an involuntary separation from the company.» What does involuntary separation mean? | Starting a new job in another town | *Being fired, against the worker's will | Leaving the job for a long holiday | Being given a big reward
exercise: Scientists call a song stuck in your head involuntary musical imagery. Find and copy the one word that tells you it was not chosen. | *involuntary | imagery | song | musical
test: «Her hand shook with an involuntary tremor.» What does involuntary suggest? | She was waving hello to a friend | *Her body moved without her choosing | She was dancing to music | She was cold and chose to shake
test: Which of these is an example of an involuntary action? | *Blinking your eyes | Choosing a film to watch | Deciding what to eat for lunch | Writing a story for homework
exam: Mia says involuntary means the same as voluntary. Is she right? | Yes, the two words mean exactly the same thing | *No, involuntary means not chosen, the opposite of voluntary | Yes, but only in science lessons | No, involuntary means very loud
